# organizations.kb — the named bodies that act in the world, and what each was set up to do.
#
# `people.kb` holds individuals and `government.kb` holds the shape of a state. This holds the
# institutions themselves: what kind of body each is, when it began, and the job it exists for.

organization | is_a=group of people arranged to pursue a shared purpose | has_part=members | has_part=rules | has_part=leadership | has_kind=international organization | has_kind=company | has_kind=charity | has_kind=university | has_kind=trade union
international organization | is_a=organization | means=one whose members are states | purpose=letting states act together on problems no state can solve alone

# --- the multilateral system ------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
united nations | is_a=international organization | purpose=maintaining international peace and cooperation | has_part=general assembly | has_part=security council | has_part=secretariat | has_part=international court of justice | located_in=New York
security council | is_a=organ of the united nations
general assembly | is_a=organ of the united nations | purpose=giving every member state one vote on the questions before it
world health organization | is_a=international organization | purpose=directing and coordinating international health work
unicef | is_a=international organization | purpose=protecting the rights and wellbeing of children
unesco | is_a=international organization | purpose=promoting cooperation in education, science and culture | causes=world heritage sites being designated
international monetary fund | is_a=international organization | purpose=lending to countries in balance of payments difficulty and monitoring the world economy | located_in=Washington
world bank | is_a=international organization
world trade organization | is_a=international organization | purpose=setting and enforcing the rules of international trade | causes=trade disputes being settled by agreed procedure
international labour organization | is_a=international organization | purpose=setting international standards for work
international atomic energy agency | is_a=international organization | purpose=promoting peaceful nuclear use and verifying that nuclear material is not diverted
world meteorological organization | is_a=international organization | purpose=coordinating weather and climate observation between states
intergovernmental panel on climate change | is_a=international body | purpose=assessing the published science of climate change for governments | causes=assessment reports that inform negotiations
european union | is_a=political and economic union | purpose=integrating the economies and some policies of its member states | has_part=european commission | has_part=council of the european union
african union | is_a=international organization | purpose=promoting cooperation and integration among African states
association of southeast asian nations | is_a=international organization | also_known_as=ASEAN | purpose=promoting regional cooperation in southeast Asia
north atlantic treaty organization | is_a=military alliance | also_known_as=NATO | purpose=collective defence of its members
opec | is_a=international organization | purpose=coordinating petroleum policy among member producing countries | causes=coordinated changes in oil supply

# --- humanitarian and standards bodies ---------------------------------------------------------------- #
international committee of the red cross | is_a=humanitarian organization | purpose=protecting victims of armed conflict | causes=the Geneva Conventions being monitored
medecins sans frontieres | is_a=humanitarian organization | also_known_as=Doctors Without Borders | purpose=providing medical care in crises and conflict
amnesty international | is_a=non governmental organization | purpose=campaigning against human rights abuses
world wide fund for nature | is_a=non governmental organization | purpose=conserving nature and reducing the most pressing threats to biodiversity
international organization for standardization | is_a=standards body | also_known_as=ISO | purpose=publishing international standards so products and processes work together
international electrotechnical commission | is_a=standards body | purpose=publishing standards for electrical and electronic technology
internet engineering task force | is_a=standards body | purpose=developing the standards that the internet runs on | causes=protocols being published as requests for comments
world wide web consortium | is_a=standards body | purpose=developing the standards of the web
ieee | is_a=professional organization | purpose=publishing standards and research in electrical engineering and computing
international olympic committee | is_a=organization | purpose=organising the Olympic Games and governing the Olympic movement
fifa | is_a=sports governing body | purpose=governing association football worldwide and organising the World Cup

# --- science and research ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ #
cern | is_a=research organization | purpose=studying particle physics with the largest accelerators | located_in=Geneva | causes=the discovery of the Higgs boson | causes=the invention of the world wide web
nasa | is_a=space agency | purpose=carrying out the civilian space programme of the United States | located_in=United States
european space agency | is_a=space agency | purpose=coordinating European space activity
isro | is_a=space agency | means=the Indian Space Research Organisation | purpose=carrying out India's space programme
royal society | is_a=learned society | purpose=promoting the natural sciences | has_property=one of the oldest scientific societies
national institutes of health | is_a=research agency | purpose=funding and conducting biomedical research
council of scientific and industrial research | is_a=research organization | purpose=running India's network of industrial and scientific laboratories

# --- what makes an organization work or fail ---------------------------------------------------------- #
charter | is_a=founding document of an organization | purpose=stating what it may do and how it decides
mandate | is_a=the authority an organization is given | purpose=setting the limits of what it may act on | causes=disputes when a body acts beyond it
non governmental organization | is_a=organization | means=one that is independent of any government | purpose=acting on a cause without state direction
charity | is_a=organization | purpose=applying its funds to a public benefit rather than to owners
trade union | is_a=organization of workers | purpose=bargaining collectively over pay and conditions | causes=a stronger position for workers than bargaining alone
cooperative | is_a=organization owned by its members | purpose=running an enterprise for the benefit of those who use it
professional body | is_a=organization | purpose=setting standards and ethics for an occupation | causes=members being removable from practice for misconduct
accountability | purpose=making an organization answerable for what it does | requires=transparency | requires=someone with the power to act on what is found
